# Haemophilia B (the "royal disease") among the descendants of Queen Victoria.
# Rogaev EI et al. (2009) Science 326(5954): 817. doi:10.1126/science.1180660
# The lines carrying the F9 mutation plus Victoria's other children. The Prussian line
# through Victoria, Princess Royal is included only as far as Henry of Prussia, whose
# marriage to his first cousin Irene of Hesse closes a loop.
# PHENO 2 = haemophiliac. PHENO 0 = status unknown or disputed. Carriers are
# phenotypically unaffected in PED; the in-app example carries the carrier flags.
# Generation 0
VICT	Queen_Victoria	0	0	2	1
VICT	Prince_Albert	0	0	1	1
# Generation 1: children of Victoria and Albert in birth order, then married-in spouses
VICT	Victoria_Princess_Royal	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	2	1
VICT	Edward_VII	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	1	1
VICT	Alice	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	2	1
VICT	Alfred	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	1	1
VICT	Helena	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	2	1
VICT	Louise	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	2	1
VICT	Arthur	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	1	1
VICT	Leopold	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	1	2
VICT	Beatrice	Prince_Albert	Queen_Victoria	2	1
VICT	Frederick_III	0	0	1	1
VICT	Louis_IV_of_Hesse	0	0	1	1
VICT	Helen_of_Waldeck	0	0	2	1
VICT	Henry_of_Battenberg	0	0	1	1
# Generation 2
VICT	Henry_of_Prussia	Frederick_III	Victoria_Princess_Royal	1	1
VICT	Victoria_of_Hesse	Louis_IV_of_Hesse	Alice	2	1
